  "solution": {
    "text": "<strong>Gabriel's synthesis :</strong> Phthalimide is reacted with <math> <mrow> <mtext>KOH</mtext></mrow> </math> to form potassium phthalimide. The potassium salt is treated with an alkyl halide. The product N-alkyl phthalimide is put to hydrolyse with hydrochloric acid, then primary amine is formed.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/39217.JPG\" style=\"width: 364px; height: 120px;\" />",
